          "id": "1df77403d861c500230115e6566da19b2d5837ea",
          "message": "test(sparq-solid): pin the container-default ACL walk contract of resolve_acl (sq-gwayp) [FABLE-5] (#2044)\n\nNew integration test tests/container_default_walk_props.rs (fresh compilation\nunit, read-only w.r.t. src/) pinning PodStore::resolve_acl's nearest-ACL-win\ncontract against the depth-4 wac_fixture() pod, via the public API only:\n\n1. the target's OWN .acl governs with AclScope::AccessTo and FULLY overrides\n   ancestors (root+mixed4 owner grants do not union into the verdict);\n2. with no own ACL, the NEAREST ancestor container with an ACL governs via\n   AclScope::Default and the walk STOPS there — the root owner grant does not\n   leak past team2/.acl (no union across levels, child->root);\n3. no ACL anywhere up to the storage root => resolve_acl None + decide denies\n   with AclStatus::NoAcl (fail-closed), even for the pod owner.\n\nAnti-vacuity witness: asserts the fixture actually EXERCISES >=2-level\ninheritance — the group doc's governing ACL is the ROOT's across the ACL-less\ngroups/ container (depth 2), plus a depth-4 witness through priv0/c4/g0/ —\nand each intermediate is proven ACL-less via its own resolve_acl scope.\nMutation-witnessed: temporarily giving groups/ an own ACL (flattening the\nfixture to one level) makes inheritance_depth_witness_at_least_two_levels\nFAIL; reverted.\n\nBead: sq-gwayp\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
          "timestamp": "2026-07-12T03:23:13Z",
