          "distinct": false,
          "id": "3ff16db1d7d1a5fa7f1ca3446f5db938f1857994",
          "message": "feat(wac-oracle): POST-Slug .acl escalation corpus + fail-closed decision assertions (sq-39kps) [FABLE-5] (#2056)\n\n* feat(wac-oracle): sparq-wac-oracle — server-independent WAC/ACP decision test-vectors + PodStore::decide runner (sq-t999y) [FABLE-5]\n\nNew opt-in leaf crate crates/sparq-wac-oracle (publish = false, dependency of\nnothing — sparq-core/sparq-engine untouched): a protocol-agnostic corpus of\nembedded WAC (.acl) + ACP (.acr) fixture pods (N-Quads, derived from the\nsparq_solid::fixture seed's policy-shape subtrees) with spec-declared\n(session, resource, mode) -> {allow, granted_modes, scope, status} rows, plus\nrun_vectors/run_fixture/run_all runners asserting PodStore::decide AND\ndecide_batch parity against every row. 47 vectors: nearest-ACL shadowing,\naccessTo-vs-default scope, group/public/authenticated/origin-pair subjects\n(WAC); cumulative inheritance, allOf agent+client pairs, deny-overrides,\nnoneOf conditional grants (ACP); fail-closed NoAcl/Transient rows.\n\nINVARIANT (result-equivalence): every fixture row equals the engine decision —\nthe fixed point the PSS-parity suite and the sq-gg0qq solid-server landing\nassert against.\n\nSole root-Cargo.toml members change per the bead's collision contract.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(wac-oracle): POST-Slug .acl escalation corpus + fail-closed decision assertions (sq-39kps) [FABLE-5]\n\nNew self-contained module crates/sparq-wac-oracle/src/escalation_corpus.rs\nenumerating the POST child-name variants that must never let a non-Control\nrequester mint or shadow a control document: the container's own `.acl` and a\nresource `.acl` shadowing an EXISTING document, in plain, percent-encoded\n(`%2E`/`%2e`), unicode compatibility-dot (U+FF0E/U+2024), and trailing-dot/space\nforms.\n\nThe corpus asserts at the DECISION layer only (no server/HTTP wiring — that is\nsq-gg0qq.5's job): for each variant it decodes the raw child to its effective\n`<stem>.acl` form, confirms it is `.acl`-shaped (Control required), and asserts\ndecide(non-control-principal, governed_resource, Mode::Control).allow == false\nvia sparq-solid's PodStore::decide. A per-entry owner-allowed anchor\n(alice DOES hold Control over each governed resource) keeps the denial\nNON-vacuous. The governed resources are materialized (the priv0/ container and\nits existing d0.ttl document), so the fail-closed result is about the principal,\nnot resource non-existence.\n\nAnti-vacuity (sq-og8u8, research/mechanized-proof-program.md §5.1-5.2): a\ngenuine-escalation cover witness (>=1 entry whose raw form evades a naive\nexact-case ends_with(\".acl\") guard yet decodes to an .acl document, still refused\nfail-closed) plus a #[cfg(kani)] domain-coverage self-check pinning the\ninteresting inputs are present, adversarial, and reachable under the bound.\n\nNON-VACUITY witnessed: flipping expect_allow -> true reddens the harness\n(dedicated test); mutation-checked that a no-op canonicalize and a\ndecode-aware naive guard each redden the suite.\n\nGates (crate-scoped): cargo test -p sparq-wac-oracle (18 + doctest green),\nclippy --all-targets -D warnings, rustdoc --all-features -D warnings,\nreadme-template 0 deviations. Single feature state (crate has no features).\nStacked on PR #2045 (the sparq-wac-oracle crate).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* ci(fv): register wac-oracle escalation Kani proof in manifest + kani.yml [FABLE-5]\n\nRecovered push of the fv-manifest registration (worker session ended while\nwaiting on a cargo kani background run). Registers domain_corpus_exhibits_a_surviving_escalation\n+ the escalation_corpus.rs #[cfg(kani)] module so the fv-select+fv-manifest\nproof-inventory GATING leg agrees with source.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(fv): close the wac-oracle escalation Kani proof in seconds — allocation-free proof-side .acl classifier [FABLE-5]\n\nThe domain_corpus_exhibits_a_surviving_escalation harness timed out at the\n20-minute FV wall-clock bound: is_acl_shaped's to_ascii_lowercase() heap-\nallocates a String per corpus entry and CBMC's string/heap modeling of that\n(x10 entries + the symbolic cover witness) blew the budget. NOT a security\ncounterexample — Kani found no surviving escalation.\n\nPROOF-ONLY fix (production is_acl_shaped untouched): the harness classifies\nentry.effective_child with is_acl_shaped_ascii_noalloc, an allocation-free\nbyte-wise equivalent (same trailing-'/' tolerance, same final-segment split,\nin-place ASCII case-fold of the .acl suffix), and asserts is_ascii() on every\ninput it classifies — under which the two predicates coincide byte-for-byte,\nso the verified property is UNCHANGED. Local run: VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL in\n~28s, 1/1 cover satisfied.\n\nAlso merges origin/main (add/add resolution keeps this branch's additions on\ntop of the merged sq-t999y crate).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
