          "distinct": false,
          "id": "ddbb31822a854be2a38708e9d0006094123aab3a",
          "message": "feat(sparq-zk): dual-leaf xsd:dateTime/xsd:date value-lane host encoders — Z-only signed scaled-epoch, fail-closed (sq-we9vs) [FABLE-5] (#2104)\n\nImplements the sq-fvztj §13 decision (research/zk-field-native-encoding.md):\nencode_datetime/encode_date with VALUE_HOOK = signed scaled-epoch (FS=3, ms),\nepochscale-folded per-lane DATATYPE_CONSTs, strict Z-only canonical predicate\n(bare/offset/24:00/leap-second/non-canonical-year/over-FS-fraction/u64-overflow\nall fail-closed, never rounded, never wrapped, never panicking). Host half only;\ncircuit member is sq-wz99x. Opt-in dual-leaf feature; default build unchanged.\nInherits INV-VL downgrade + CR-G8 / sq-qhy4 audit obligation — NO soundness claim.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
          "timestamp": "2026-07-12T09:43:10Z",
